  "caveats": [
    "Concurrent load: another agent ran the CLI pipeline benchmark on the same machine during this run (load average 10.51 on 16 logical cores when recorded); timings are from a shared, moderately loaded laptop.",
    "Dev-mode server: numbers reflect `mix phx.server` with MIX_ENV=dev (code reloader, debug logging, esbuild/tailwind watchers), not a production release.",
    "The host slept for about 10.6 h between the first server launch (2026-11-07T23:36:01Z) and the next command; the first attempt was discarded anyway (see next item) and every reported number comes from the fresh run on 2026-11-08 between 10:23Z and 10:26Z.",
    "First attempt (run1-aborted/) hit two script bugs: `.artifact-row` also matches the Company-home harness list, so the package locators had to be scoped to #package-panel, and #nav-privacy sits inside the collapsed #workspace-tools <details>. Both were fixed in bench/portal.cjs and the whole flow was rerun on a brand-new workspace.",
    "Start-to-ready of the measured fresh-workspace boot is an upper bound (6.964 s) because the readiness poll started after the server already answered; the same-shell timed restarts (3 warm, 3 fresh workspaces) are the precise figures.",
    "The evaluation card renders the qualification text as \"Recorded runtime qualification: false\" (inside a collapsed <details>, opened for the screenshot); the literal string \"Runtime qualified: false\" from test/browser/smoke.cjs does not occur in the current markup.",
    "Evidence-tab navigation samples use the real route /?view=evidence; the tab switch from Home was measured separately as an in-page click latency.",
    "Action latencies are DOM-signal based (click event to first matching DOM mutation), measured inside the page; node-side wall times are reported alongside and are 20-50 ms higher.",
    "The run-1 beam process RSS (100604 KiB) was read after about 10 h of idling including host sleep; it is listed only for completeness.",
    "ps rss is reported in KiB; MB values are derived (KiB*1024/1e6)."
  ]
